  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "$7$ is prime **or** $2$ is less than $5.$\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $R:7\\text{\u00a0is prime}$\n\n- $P:2\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}5$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{\u00a0is prime}}_{\u23df}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{2\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}5}_{\u23df}}_{P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R\u2228P.$",
